more gridlock in Syria the latest convoy  bringing food and supplies to the civil  war ravaged city of Aleppo is being held  at the syria-turkey border the convoy  had been given clearance to leave Turkey  but did not have the go-ahead to make  delivery Secretary of State John Kerry's  asking his Russian counterpart to  pressure the Syrian government to end  the delay meanwhile in Aleppo Syria's  besieged largest city people are simply  trying to get on with their lives  Elizabeth Palmer is there with the  latest Elizabeth good morning good  morning you know four people trapped in  a war zone the ordinary simple pleasures  of normal life are especially sweet and  nothing says normal on a hot day like a  swimming pool believe it or not right  now on the government controlled side of  the city several of Aleppo swimming  pools are open for business in the  streets people socialize they do odd  jobs even SAS the camera and it all  helps to blot out the violence and the  fear but nothing can disguise the ugly  scar that divides this city between the  government and its armed opposition 13  year old aya el Hassan is giving us a  tour of her neighborhood of ally done  right on the front lawn this curtain  here what's that for good mouse and then  out here is David the snipers just a few  hundred yards away our opposition  fighters who have aimed their weapons at  Syrian army positions deep in this  neighborhood did you lose some friends  in this war criminal fuzzy Fattah yes  I've lost many she says some were killed  by mortars or snipers some just left the  country aya like everyone who lives here  can remember when fellow citizens of  Aleppo lived down that road beyond the  barriers not men with guns what was the  worst time you can remember wasn't scary  little one night she says a mortar  actually landed in our house it was a  concrete apartment like these so a  miracle no one was killed with courage  beyond her years Aya's  her eye on the future no I want my son  pole again she says and at peace and as  for the people on the other side the  opposition side of that sniper shield we  weren't able to meet them because we're  not allowed to cross the line but they  are besieged at the moment by the Syrian  army and are in really desperate straits  they're the ones who are waiting for the  aid that is stuck at the Turkish border  Anthony in vinita Elizabeth Palmer and  Aleppo Syria this morning thank you
 

